The runbook told readers to run `python refresh_data.py`, a file that has never
existed in the repository; the scheduled workflow used the same wrong command
and failed on all 18 runs between 2026-02-22 and 2026-06-21. Corrected to
`python -m pipeline.refresh` throughout, with a note so the discrepancy is not
read as a typo.

Add Section 13 covering the production target: Fly.io, one machine plus a
volume, and why it cannot be more than one — the Keyword Explorer writes cache
tables to the live database, and SQLite WAL is single-writer with no cross-host
coordination, which also rules out serverless.

Also document APP_FEEDBACK_PATH, APP_HOST, APP_DOCS_DIR and BACKUP_DIR, and drop
SUPPORTED_FISCAL_YEARS — that variable appears nowhere in the codebase, and its
documented default of 2024,2025,2026 implied a fiscal-year limit that does not
exist.
