+## 13. Production Hosting -- Fly.io
+
+The production target is **Fly.io: one machine with a persistent volume**.
+
+### Why a single machine
+
+This is a constraint, not a preference. The Keyword Explorer -- which serves the
+default landing page at `/` -- builds its cache by issuing `DROP TABLE` /
+`CREATE TABLE` / `INSERT` against the live database, so `dod_budget.sqlite` must
+be **writable at request time**. SQLite in WAL mode permits one writer and does
+not coordinate across hosts, so:
+
+- The app runs exactly one always-on machine (`min_machines_running = 1`,
+  `auto_stop_machines = false`).
+- It **cannot scale horizontally** without replacing the storage layer. Two
+  instances on separate volumes would serve divergent Explorer caches; two
+  sharing one network volume would corrupt it.
+- Serverless platforms are unusable here, despite this looking like a small
+  read-mostly API, because function filesystems are ephemeral.
+
+### Layout
+
+```
+ghcr.io/wschosta/dod-budget-analysis:<sha>
+        |  flyctl deploy --image
+        v
+Fly machine x1
+  |- /app     application code, replaced wholesale on each deploy
+  \- /data    volume: dod_budget.sqlite + feedback.json
+```
+
+Mutable state lives on the volume, never in the image. `APP_DB_PATH` and
+`APP_FEEDBACK_PATH` both point at `/data` for exactly this reason -- anything
+written under `/app` is discarded on the next deploy.
+
+### First-time setup
+
+```bash
+fly apps create dod-budget-explorer
+fly volumes create dod_budget_data --size 10 --region iad
+# Add FLY_API_TOKEN as a GitHub Actions repository secret
+```
+
+Then seed the database, which is *not* built during deploy (it needs network
+access to DoD sites and considerable time):
+
+```bash
+python scripts/run_pipeline.py            # produces dod_budget.sqlite
+ls -lh dod_budget.sqlite                  # size the volume at roughly 3x this
+fly sftp shell                            # put it at /data/dod_budget.sqlite
+```
+
+The 3x headroom covers the WAL file, the Explorer cache tables, and one refresh
+in flight.
+
+### Deploying
+
+`deploy.yml` runs automatically on push to `main`: it verifies CI passed, builds
+and pushes the image to GHCR, deploys it with `flyctl deploy --image`, then
+smoke-tests the live URL. Until `FLY_API_TOKEN` exists the deploy job logs a
+warning and exits cleanly, and the smoke test is skipped rather than run against
+a URL that was never deployed.
+
+Configuration lives in `fly.toml`; the decision record with rejected
+alternatives is in `docs/HOSTING_DECISION.md`.
+
+### Scheduled workflows go dormant
+
+GitHub disables scheduled workflows after 60 days without repository activity.
+This already happened once: `refresh-data.yml` stopped firing after 2026-06-21.
+Pushing commits does **not** restore them -- re-enable each one by hand under
+**Actions** in the GitHub UI, and check that they are still running after any
+long quiet period.
+
